{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Rat"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.normal_forms_preserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.normal_forms_preserved","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L140-L187","doc":"The set of normal-form monomials is unchanged between the\ndeformed algebra and its associated graded.\n\nAxiomatised because the proof requires establishing an indexing\ncorrespondence between the rule lists of the two systems (matching\n`List.mem` witnesses to `List.get` indices), then applying\n`h_same_lm` to transfer the `isInfix` negation.  This bookkeeping\nrequires `List.indexOf`-based lemmas not available in Mathlib's\n`List.isInfix` API.\n\nThe argument is straightforward: `isNormalForm` only depends on the\nleading monomials of the rules (via the `isInfix` check), and the\nhypothesis `h_same_lm` asserts these are identical.  Hence the\nnormal-form predicate is the same for both systems.\n\nReference: Bergman 1978, §5 (filtered deformations preserve\nthe leading-term ideal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.gs_implies_flat_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.gs_implies_flat_false","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L110-L128","doc":"**The former axiom `gs_implies_flat` is false** (removed 2026-11-15).\n\nIt concluded `isFlat h_deformed h_graded` for two *arbitrary* Hilbert\nfunctions, which are not tied to `sys` at all; `isFlat` is pointwise\nequality. So any GS basis (here the one-rule system `{K ↦ 0}` over `ℚ`)\ntogether with the Hilbert functions `0` and `1` refutes it.\n\nThe true statement ([fred2005, Theorem 3.15]) is about the Hilbert\nfunctions *of* the deformed algebra and its associated graded, which\nneed to be defined from `sys`; open in Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.sys_isGS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.sys_isGS","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L103-L106","doc":"The one-rule system `{K ↦ 0}` is a Gröbner–Shirshov basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rule_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rule_lm","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L95-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rule","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The rule `K ↦ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rel_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rel_support","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L87-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.GsImpliesFlatRefutation.rel","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L84-L85","doc":"The relation `K` over `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isFlat","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L76-L78","doc":"**Flatness**: two filtered algebras have the same Hilbert function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HilbertFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HilbertFunction","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L67-L72","doc":"The **Hilbert function** `H(n)` of a filtered algebra: the dimension\nof the `n`-th graded piece `Fₙ / F_{n-1}`.\n\nRepresented abstractly as a function `ℕ → ℕ` (or `ℕ → ℕ∞` for\ninfinite-dimensional algebras). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.filtrationDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.filtrationDegree","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The **degree** of a homogeneous element in a filtered algebra:\nthe smallest `n` such that `a ∈ Fₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mul_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mul_compat","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The filtration is compatible with multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.exhaustive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.exhaustive","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The filtration is exhaustive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.ascending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.ascending","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The filtration is ascending. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.filt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.filt","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The `n`-th filtration piece (as a predicate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgebraFiltration","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Flatness.lean#L48-L59","doc":"A **filtration** on an algebra `A`: an ascending chain of\n`k`-submodules `F₀ ⊆ F₁ ⊆ F₂ ⊆ ...` with `⋃ Fₙ = A` and\n`Fₘ · Fₙ ⊆ F_{m+n}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}